tr_by=hand
why=pelt#49, ruling #113: the option's cd is the command cd: its status and its diagnostic (a directory it cannot enter: cd's failure, said through the command's redirections, as bash 5.3, black-box, notes/sh23-evidence/refs/base2/bash-i-autocd/p08-status), the command's assignments for the call only (bash, black-box, notes/sh23-evidence/refs/base2/bash-i-autocd/p11-env), its redirections around it, and a function named cd runs when one is defined (bash calls it with -- NAME, black-box, notes/sh23-evidence/refs/base/bash-i-autocd/p06-cdfn; zsh the built-in), so lope's cd records the jump. command ./dir is the plain 126 here (command asks for the utility, as pelt#42's hook is not called for it), where bash and zsh go to the directory. In ( ) and a pipeline stage the shell stays. Written by hand from pelt trunk's answers to the explicit session (notes/sh23-evidence/handtr.py)
